<diagram>
  <annotations>
    <annotation id="prefigure-tp-solar-tilt-figure" speech2="A side view of the roof, cut by the vertical plane through the top of the dome and the point P 0. The grey curve is the roof, falling away from its top on the z axis. The panel is a thick dark blue segment tangent to the roof at P 0. A dashed blue horizontal line starts at P 0, and the angle theta between it and the panel is the tilt. A blue arrow k points straight up from P 0 and a red arrow, the upward normal 1 comma negative 3 comma 4, is perpendicular to the panel. The angle between these two arrows is the same angle theta, about 38 degrees.">
      <grouped>prefigure-tp-solar-tilt-figure</grouped>
      <position>1</position>
      <children>
        <active>prefigure-tp-solar-tilt-st-roof</active>
